{"author":{"id":"2de4467f26c42fb223f4d3ddd5611e7c0513d3daae4c1dc315de039036bc997d"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1775412318,"nonce":"sEqPJ9XET3OKgyE6djVyTNs+2Xw=","title":"Sidenote hydration error on long/complex footnotes","message":"## Problem\n\nBlog posts with long or structurally complex footnotes (multi-paragraph, numbered lists, nested bullets) cause a React hydration error:\n\n```\nIn HTML, \u003cdiv\u003e cannot be a descendant of \u003cp\u003e\n```\n\nTriggered on `the-blueberries-of-wrath.md` footnotes `[^2]` through `[^7]`, all of which exceed the 200-char `maxNoteLength` truncation threshold in `useTruncatableNote`.\n\n## Root cause\n\nServer/client mismatch in `Sidenote` component. `useMediaQuery` initializes `isDesktop = false` on the server. On the client, after mount, it becomes `true` for desktop viewports. For notes exceeding 200 chars, `shouldTruncate` flips from `false` (server) to `true` (client), producing a different React tree (truncated text + \"more\" button) than what was server-rendered. React reports this as a structural hydration error.\n\nAdditionally, `extractTextContent()` in `remark-sidenotes.ts` flattens all block structure (lists, paragraphs) into a single concatenated string, losing formatting. A 4-item numbered list rendered as a flat string in a narrow sidenote margin is poor UX regardless of the hydration bug.\n\n## Proposed fix (two parts)\n\n### 1. Per-footnote opt-out marker\n\nAdd a convention: footnote definitions starting with `!` (e.g. `[^3]: ! This stays as a footnote`) are skipped by the sidenote conversion in `remark-sidenotes.ts`. The `!` prefix is stripped before display. This gives authors per-footnote control over which notes become sidenotes vs. traditional bottom-of-page footnotes.\n\nImplementation: in Pass 1 of `remark-sidenotes.ts`, check if the extracted text content starts with `!` (after trimming). If so, do not splice the `footnoteDefinition` from the AST — let it pass through to the standard footnote rendering pipeline. Strip the `!` prefix from the definition content.\n\n### 2. Fix the hydration mismatch\n\nMake truncation logic SSR-compatible. Options:\n- Always truncate long notes on server too (render truncated HTML, hydrate to match)\n- Use `suppressHydrationWarning` on the affected span\n- Defer truncation rendering to a `useEffect` with consistent initial state\n\n### Affected files\n\n- `lib/remark-sidenotes.ts` — footnote extraction and conversion\n- `components/sidenote.tsx` — `useTruncatableNote` hook, `renderContent()`\n- `hooks/use-media-query.ts` — `isDesktop` initialization\n\n### Reproduction\n\n1. `npm run dev`\n2. Navigate to `/blog/the-blueberries-of-wrath`\n3. Open browser console — hydration error appears","files":null}]}